Hey, [~accountid:712020:a7a7d4bc-10ca-44a0-a22e-fa8752330abd] 

Thank you for relevant questions.



{quote}is it for Rides only or does it affect the Bolt Food app as well?{quote}

As far as I am aware this applies to both the Food app and the Rider app (so for both eaters and riders).

{quote}I see you have a plan for reducing the number of sensitive emails sent to unverified addresses. Can you walk me through it?{quote}

Infosec intends to push for it, mostly due to concerns of potential legal action against us as there is personal data sent to these addresses as well as complaints of email abuse due to unsolicited emails to people who are not our customers.

No concrete plans that we are aware of, but Identity has some actions towards this planned later this year. [~accountid:60c842452bd2140069d30e58] can you comment on them?

{quote}Will we have an “unsubscribe” button for these emails?{quote}

Until we stop sending emails to unverified addresses, infosec would advise including _why am I receiving these emails/unsubscribe_ links to be included in all new email messages (to measure the extent of unsolicited email issue).

{quote}Any alternative channels for sending these kinds of messages, e.g. in-app?{quote}

It might be possible to send a [Push message|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/3545007154/Push+channel+characteristics] instead, however by its nature the push message will not be as informative as email. 

[~accountid:6426ea8f57f0c028e2f7cf7f] Could it be feasible to use push notifications as an alternative for users with unverified email address? 

{quote}Do we have any similar features? Have we received a lot of backlash re sending emails to unverified email addresses?{quote}

We have received some backslash, infosec email gets a few (<10) requests every month to stop sending emails to complainer’s email address. Most of the time people emailing us claim that they have never used our services. 

{quote}have we thought about mandatory email verification for all users? (I suspect I know your answer already, but I have to ask 🙂 ){quote}

Mandatory email for all users will probably remain unfeasible, as our customers do not necessarily have an email address on some markets. However it would be good to mandate email verification for users wishing to receive email notifications from us or on markets where sending such emails (e.g invoices) is mandatory.

{quote}is it for Rides only or does it affect the Bolt Food app as well?{quote}

both.

{quote}I see you have a plan for reducing the number of sensitive emails sent to unverified addresses. Can you walk me through it?

Identity has some actions towards this planned later this year. [~accountid:60c842452bd2140069d30e58] can you comment on them?{quote}

I will create a Slack channel on the topic to bring some clarity for everyone on current status on our plans to address/ mitigate it over time.

{quote}Until we stop sending emails to unverified addresses, infosec would advise including _why am I receiving these emails/unsubscribe_ links to be included in all new email messages (to measure the extent of unsolicited email issue).{quote}

Indeed I think we can do something along those lines to make the current process for unwanted emails unsubscribtion a bit less user-hostile.

{quote}have we thought about mandatory email verification for all users?{quote}

It is extreemely unlikely due to the friction involved, however with our plans to move away from phone number as primary authentication method, the % of verified email users will increase significantly and this issue will naturally die down over time.

