Trainings are assigned to drivers in the following cases:

# *As a warning* - before their Driver Score or Acceptance/Confirmation rate falls below a certain threshold (the threshold is now low enough to block the driver, instead, drivers are educated so that they won’t be blocked in the future)
# *Acceptance rate and Driver Score training/guidance* - when the score falls below the allowed threshold (thresholds are defined locally?)
## {color:#bf2600}*Thresholds are defined locally yes, per market, usually done through the Driver Quality team, between Local Ops and Quality.*{color}
# *Safety cases* - Can you clarify this a bit more? Are the trainings assigned in every safety event or only in the ones mentioned [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4500422657/Safety+Contextual+Guidance#How-are-drivers-enrolled-to-this%3F]? Also, if the driver has not done the same guidance in the last 7 days or 50 orders, they will be assigned safety training (is this for education purposes or something else?)
## {color:#bf2600}*At the moment, contextual guidance is provided to drivers in the following situations:*{color}
### {color:#bf2600}*Unsafe Driving (CS closes ticket regarding it,  then guide is triggered)*{color}
### {color:#bf2600}*Offline Trips (which as I understood is already being investigated separately)*{color}
### {color:#bf2600}*Ride’s Too Short (when drivers accept rides, start, and finish them within 30 seconds), when this happens, a guide is triggered to them.*{color}

*How to check assigned guides?*

* Where in Admin Panel? What is the path to get there?
** {color:#bf2600}*Assigned trainings for a driver can be seen under Driver Profile in new Admin Panel. It’s visible under Trainings tab. (Right side on the image)*{color}
** !image-20240129-131207.png|width=1680,height=194!

* Possible types:
** context_guidance_acceptance_rate
** Can you list all possible types?
*** {color:#bf2600}*CONTEXT_GUIDANCE_SAFETY = "context_guidance_safety",*{color}
{color:#bf2600}*CONTEXT_GUIDANCE_ACCEPTANCE_RATE = "context_guidance_acceptance_rate",*{color}
{color:#bf2600}*CONTEXT_GUIDANCE_OFFLINE_TRIP = "context_guidance_offline_trip",*{color}
{color:#bf2600}*CONTEXT_GUIDANCE_RIDE_TOO_SHORT_TIME = "context_guidance_ride_too_short_time"*{color}
* The case should be escalated to Tech Support if something is wrong, as agents cannot manually reassign the training to drivers
** What are possible issues that drivers may encounter? How to troubleshoot those issues?
*** {color:#bf2600}*Usually, the main issue is that the guide is not being completed/block isn’t removed. In this situation, a driver could be suggested to ensure they’re tapping on the right side of the screen to complete the guide (since it reads what step you’re on and where do you press to proceed) and/or update their app version to the latest one, ensuring they have good enough internet access.*{color}

Regarding the onboarding guidance - new drivers are assigned with these trainings which are presented as in-app stories, but can we predict possible issues with this or there are none?

* {color:#bf2600}*So far we haven’t received any issues regarding onboarding guidance, drivers once complete the 1st day module of the guide, they can go online (except in a few countries where they can go online regardless if the guide is completed). The next 4 guides they receive over the 4 days are optional for them to complete.*{color}





